Ladybird buffers bounded primitive values and minimal object summaries
for console history. Ordinary objects keep only their internal class
name, and DOM elements keep their bounded name and ID. Terminal output
keeps its bounded property previews. Live DevTools messages still use
expandable object references.

Ladybird deliberately keeps its history free of object references.
Blink retains arguments in V8ConsoleMessage::createForConsoleAPI and
creates protocol objects in V8ConsoleMessage::wrapArguments. WebKit
retains ScriptArguments in ConsoleMessage, and wraps their values when
sending a message to the frontend. Gecko stores console events in
ConsoleAPIStorage.recordEvent, and creates grips through the console
actor. These engines can inspect retained values when tools open.
Ladybird instead replays summaries, preserving its retention policy.
